# Extra leak patterns for the pre-commit hook. Copy to `leak-patterns.local` and edit:
#
#     cp scripts/hooks/leak-patterns.local.example scripts/hooks/leak-patterns.local
#
# `leak-patterns.local` is gitignored on purpose. This repo was extracted from a private
# one, so the terms worth blocking are customer names, internal hostnames, and ticket
# prefixes — and a public list of the names you are hiding publishes them.
#
# One extended-regex (grep -E) pattern per line, case-sensitive. Blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored. Keep them anchored enough not to fire on ordinary prose:
# a bare company name that is also an English word will block every commit until someone
# deletes the file, and a check people delete is worse than one that never existed.
#
# Do not use `(?i)` — BSD grep honours it, GNU grep does not, so a pattern tested on a Mac
# silently matches nothing on Linux. Write `[Aa]cme` instead.

# Internal ticket prefixes
# \b(ABC|DEF)-[0-9]+

# Internal hosts and domains
# internal\.example\.com
# connector\.example\.net

# Customer, tenant, and store names
# acmeretail
# northwind
